    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>a point inside a triangle of a mesh cut along its intersections with other triangles, defined by mesh vertices in the exact coordinates that the boolean&apos;s predicates take, with the same ids: either a vertex, or the point where a segment crosses the plane of a triangle (an edge-triangle intersection found by <ref refid="group__MathGroup_1ga4b162fc9a97cef14dfdf9a7dfc6bf34f" kindref="member">doTriangleSegmentIntersect</ref>), or the crossing of two cuts of the triangle, where the planes of two other triangles and its own one meet; the coordinates are below 2^30 by absolute value, as <ref refid="group__MathGroup_1ga1d477d2bd0d97e5a7ee1a9b3e62d06cc" kindref="member">getToIntConverter</ref> makes them, which the widths of the exact integers and the error bounds of the predicates rely on, and an id stands for one vertex with the same coordinates in every point </para>
    </detaileddescription>
